WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 2 Leader Video
Unit 1, Lesson 2: Faith

1
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.810
So, several years ago, I was in a brand new apartment.

2
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:14.810
I woke up in the middle of the night to do something, I don't remember what it was.

3
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:23.810
As I went back to bed, I rammed my toe so hard into the bed frame that I ended up breaking my toe.

4
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:26.810
I didn't know I broke it until I woke up the next morning.

5
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:27.810
It was black and blue.

6
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.810
My whole foot was all messed up.

7
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.810
And I limped around for days.

8
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:35.810
There was nothing that could be done about it because I just simply broke my toe.

9
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:39.810
The bed wasn't new, but the apartment was.

10
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.810
And when I woke up, it was pitch black.

11
00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.810
I couldn't see a thing.

12
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:48.810
So naturally, I was so disoriented, didn't know where I was, didn't know what was going on,

13
00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:52.810
that I forgot where the bed was because I forgot where I was.

14
00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:57.810
Now, see, growing up in my younger days as an early baby Christian,

15
00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.810
that's kind of how I thought of faith.

16
00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:05.810
I thought of faith as sort of this wandering in the darkness trying to figure something out,

17
00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:11.810
hoping that I don't stub my toe and hope I don't do something kind of dumb.

18
00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:18.810
And in reality, in my life, I actually did stub my toe to the point where I walked away for quite some time.

19
00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:26.810
And as I came back to the church, I realized something that faith is not at all like wandering in the darkness.

20
00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.810
And what I've discovered is that so many students still kind of have that belief

21
00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.810
that it's just either attaching themselves to what their parents believe

22
00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:38.810
and simply just going along with something or literally wandering around in the darkness,

23
00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:42.810
hoping that what they believe is somehow true

24
00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:46.810
and that somehow in the end of all things, when this life ends,

25
00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.810
that they'll find out that it is actually true.

26
00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:54.810
What's interesting, though, is that John says something in the very end of his gospel

27
00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:59.810
that starts to speak to us about really what faith actually is.

28
00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.810
And it's in John chapter 20, verses 30 and 31.

29
00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.810
And John says this,

30
00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:09.810
Jesus did many other miracles or miraculous signs in the presence of his disciples,

31
00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.810
which are not recorded in this book,

32
00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:15.810
but these are written that you may believe

33
00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.810
that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God,

34
00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:22.810
and that by believing you may have life in his name.

35
00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:26.810
What's interesting is what John says to you is that these miraculous signs,

36
00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:30.810
all of these things that John has recorded in his gospel

37
00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:34.810
are so that you might believe were given reasons.

38
00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:41.810
And what's fascinating about the gospel of John is the seven miraculous signs that John gives,

39
00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:44.810
starting with Jesus turning water into wine

40
00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:50.810
and then ending with this magnitude kind of a miracle with the raising of Lazarus.

41
00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:55.810
And then if you want to include the eighth one of Jesus' own resurrection,

42
00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.810
is that time after time, John sets it up

43
00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:07.810
so that we see increasing in measure all these signs that Jesus is exactly who he says he is.

44
00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.810
And this is what we want students to actually get,

45
00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:16.810
that biblical faith is trust based on evidence

46
00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:19.810
and that translates really into a deeper relationship.

47
00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.810
I mean think about the relationships that you have.

48
00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:26.810
You don't just blindly trust somebody that you don't know,

49
00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:30.810
but the more you get to know somebody, the more you trust them.

50
00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.810
The more you trust them, the deeper that relationship starts to go.

51
00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.810
And this is sort of how relationships work.

52
00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.810
It's no different with our relationship with Christ.

53
00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:44.810
The more we know who he is, the more we know about what's going on

54
00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:47.810
and what the gospel is, the more we can trust

55
00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:52.810
and the more reason we have to trust in what God is doing through Christ.

56
00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:57.810
And the more that we do that, the deeper our relationship with him goes.

57
00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:02.810
And this is exactly why we start in this lesson

58
00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:05.810
with this idea of your students trust between friends.

59
00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:08.810
We want them to get that sense of what that looks like

60
00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:13.810
because our best and deepest relationships are built on a sense of trust,

61
00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.810
a deep sense of trust.

62
00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:20.810
And we have that because that person has either continually provided reasons to trust them

63
00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:23.810
or maybe not reasons to trust them.

64
00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:26.810
So we want our students to be able to see how that works.

65
00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:29.810
And what's really even more fascinating I think

66
00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.810
is when we start thinking about what faith is and how this works

67
00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:36.810
we naturally kind of find ourselves in Hebrews 11, right?

68
00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:37.810
Hebrews 11 1.

69
00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.810
Now faith is being sure of what we hope for

70
00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:42.810
and certain of what we do not see.

71
00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:44.810
This is what the ancients were commended for.

72
00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:49.810
And then the writer of Hebrews goes through that huge wall of faith

73
00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.810
of all these people that had the right kind of faith.

74
00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:57.810
And we use this verse as sort of the foundational piece of what faith means, right?

75
00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:01.810
Being sure of what we hope for and certain of what we do not see.

76
00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:03.810
Well, that word's certain.

77
00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:07.810
The word actually means, or it has with it,

78
00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:11.810
the idea of a foundation or substructure.

79
00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:14.810
So think of it this way. It's a basement.

80
00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:19.810
The idea that the writer is talking about is the basement in your home.

81
00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.810
When you walk downstairs into your basement,

82
00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.810
if you have one or if you've ever walked into a basement,

83
00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:30.810
you generally don't fear that the whole house is going to cave in on you, right?

84
00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.810
Because you've walked down to a basement,

85
00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.810
it has these huge metal beams and these metal poles

86
00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.810
and they're driven into the cement, into the ground

87
00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:42.810
and the whole house is being held up by these beams and this basement.

88
00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:46.810
And when you walk downstairs, you don't think anything of it.

89
00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:47.810
Why?

90
00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:50.810
Because the house is built out of solid foundation

91
00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.810
and if foundation in the house is cracked,

92
00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.810
the house is starting to be no good

93
00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:59.810
and you can't really do anything in the house until you fix the foundation.

94
00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:02.810
So that's what the writer is saying.

95
00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.810
He's saying that it's so sure, so fundamental

96
00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:09.810
that you can walk into a house and feel totally confident

97
00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.810
so much so that you don't even think about it.

98
00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.810
That's what faith is.

99
00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:16.810
It's that foundational piece of what we do not see.

100
00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.810
It's assurance of it.

101
00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.810
And in fact, if you take it one step deeper,

102
00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:25.810
the root word comes from the idea of an idea

103
00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:28.810
or one who stands immovable.

104
00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:30.810
It cannot be moved at all.

105
00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:35.810
One who is so rock solid and so dug into a foundation

106
00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.810
that it can't be moved.

107
00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:41.810
That is what our faith is and that's what we want students to be able to see.

108
00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:43.810
I mean, think about it for a second.

109
00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:45.810
I was just thinking about this the other day.

110
00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:48.810
Why did Jesus keep his wounds?

111
00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:51.810
Why would Jesus, he's Jesus.

112
00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:55.810
He resurrects and yet in the end of John's gospel,

113
00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.810
he shows Thomas his wounds.

114
00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.810
Thomas wants to see them.

115
00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:05.810
He wants to see for himself what it is that Jesus...

116
00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.810
Why? It's Jesus.

117
00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:08.810
He's resurrected.

118
00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.810
What more evidence do you need?

119
00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:11.810
Right?

120
00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:13.810
But Jesus keeps his wounds.

121
00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.810
And I've always found that really fascinating

122
00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.810
that out of all things that Jesus could have done,

123
00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:20.810
we'd be like, well, I'm going to fix these wounds

124
00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:22.810
because why would I want to have these holes in my wrist

125
00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:24.810
and this gash in my side?

126
00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:27.810
Why would I want to keep those?

127
00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:32.810
One more reason, even if it was just for Thomas,

128
00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:36.810
one more reason to show that this is who I am

129
00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:40.810
and I've done exactly what I said I was going to do.

130
00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:43.810
So, faith.

131
00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:47.810
We want our students to really understand the deep roots of faith

132
00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:50.810
that it's not wandering in the darkness,

133
00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:53.810
but it's assurance and evidence of belief.

134
00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:56.810
So our small group time should be something

135
00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:59.810
that students can take a step back

136
00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.810
and think about it and discuss with each other

137
00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:05.810
what it really means to have faith.

138
00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:07.810
And I want your students to start

139
00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:09.810
and you should encourage your students to start

140
00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:12.810
thinking about, well, do I have my own faith

141
00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.810
or am I still just believing what my parents believed

142
00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:17.810
or what other people have told me to believe

143
00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:21.810
or am I starting to now believe things on my own

144
00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.810
based on what I'm now discovering

145
00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:27.810
and that starts with asking your students,

146
00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:30.810
have they considered the evidence?

147
00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:34.810
Have they considered all of the tools that are in here,

148
00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:39.810
especially that God has given us to figure out

149
00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:42.810
is what Jesus did and what God is doing

150
00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:45.810
and the whole of salvation history?

151
00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:47.810
Is that enough?

152
00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:51.810
So what we're talking about is finding a space

153
00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:55.810
where students can start to make their faith their own.

154
00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:58.810
It's easy for us as leaders to stand up in front of

155
00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:00.810
a bunch of students and tell them about our faith

156
00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.810
and read through scripture and give them

157
00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.810
an interpretation of what our faith looks like

158
00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:08.810
and what faith they ought to have based on our faith.

159
00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.810
But it's a whole different thing

160
00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.810
and the thing that we want you to start

161
00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:15.810
to encourage students to this transfer

162
00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:18.810
of what we're telling them to believe

163
00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.810
and what they believe based on the evidence

164
00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:23.810
that they're discovering on their own begins to happen

165
00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:26.810
is we want you to create a space

166
00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:30.810
where students can invest, they can pursue on their own,

167
00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:32.810
they can go back to the idea of questions,

168
00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.810
they can ask the right questions

169
00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:36.810
or ask any questions for that matter

170
00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:40.810
so that the evidence that's here in scripture

171
00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.810
will come right off the page and into their lives.

172
00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:45.810
That's the kind of faith that sticks.

173
00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:48.810
That's the kind of faith that they'll take with them to college.

174
00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:51.810
That's the kind of faith that we want them to have.

175
00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:54.810
We don't want to just them to accept what we're telling them.

176
00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:57.810
We want them to discover that what we're telling them

177
00:09:57.810 --> 00:09:59.810
is actually true.

178
00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:02.810
So three things to keep in mind.

179
00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.810
One, drive home the fact that biblical faith

180
00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:06.810
is not without evidence.

181
00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:09.810
Biblical faith is not without evidence.

182
00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.810
Number two, that Jesus has taken significant time

183
00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:15.810
and energy to give us that evidence.

184
00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:17.810
And finally, number three,

185
00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.810
for students considering the evidence,

186
00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.810
it opens the door to a much deeper

187
00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.810
and more meaningful relationship

188
00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:26.810
with the creator of the world.

